        "abstract": "We present a low overhead technique that can be used to offset both large systematic and random process delay variation in the near-threshold voltage operation region. We present an analysis of this this technique applied to a 65nm CMOS self synchronous FPGA that is capable of operation from 2.0V to 0.37V. By using dual voltage supplies, we can offset gate-level pipeline stages that show large delay variation, to achieve energy savings per operation of up to 102x for a 200 stage pipeline.",
