                "lastName": "Kuroda"
            }
        ],
        "abstract": "We propose 3-D integrated mobile phone system utilizing an inductive-coupling link. To realize energy efficient 3-die stacking, a slew-rate controlled footer switch scheme and a superposition of magnetic field scheme are proposed. By using a place-and-route model of a coil, we demonstrate that a commercial layout tool can handle the inductive-coupling link module successfully. Performance of the proposed circuit is estimated as 5.184Gbps/ch and 6.1pJ/b for 2-die stacking and 9.5pJ/b for 3-die stacking. The area efficiency is 592μm<sup xmlns:mml=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\">2</sup>/Gbps, which is 1/330 of the prior art.",
        "keywords": {
            "IEEE Keywords": [
                "Coils",
                "Program processors",
                "Stacking",
                "Transmitters",
                "Layout",
                "CMOS integrated circuits",
                "Mobile handsets"
            ],
